[
  {
    "chunk_id": "LEGAL_VENDOR_LEGAL_GUIDELINES_CHUNK_001",
    "text": "**NovaCore Technologies Pvt. Ltd.  \nVENDOR LEGAL GUIDELINES**\n\n| **Document ID**      | LEG-GDL-002                            |\n|----------------------|----------------------------------------|\n| **Department**       | Legal                                  |\n| **Document Type**    | Guidelines                             |\n| **Policy Title**     | Vendor Legal and Compliance Guidelines |\n| **Version**          | 2026                                   |\n| **Effective Date**   | 01-Apr-2026                            |\n| **Owner Department** | Legal                                  |",
    "metadata": {
      "department": "Legal",
      "document_name": "Vendor_Legal_Guidelines",
      "document_type": "DOCX",
      "source_file": "data/raw/Legal/Vendor_Legal_Guidelines.docx",
      "policy_title": "Vendor Legal and Compliance Guidelines",
      "version": "2026",
      "effective_date": "01-Apr-2026",
      "owner_department": "Legal",
      "document_id": "LEGAL_VENDOR_LEGAL_GUIDELINES",
      "section": "Document Introduction",
      "chunk_id": "LEGAL_VENDOR_LEGAL_GUIDELINES_CHUNK_001"
    }
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "LEGAL_VENDOR_LEGAL_GUIDELINES_CHUNK_002",
    "text": "These guidelines define legal due diligence, documentation, contract review, compliance, data protection, intellectual property, single-source considerations, and vendor compliance expectations.",
    "metadata": {
      "department": "Legal",
      "document_name": "Vendor_Legal_Guidelines",
      "document_type": "DOCX",
      "source_file": "data/raw/Legal/Vendor_Legal_Guidelines.docx",
      "policy_title": "Vendor Legal and Compliance Guidelines",
      "version": "2026",
      "effective_date": "01-Apr-2026",
      "owner_department": "Legal",
      "document_id": "LEGAL_VENDOR_LEGAL_GUIDELINES",
      "section": "1. Purpose",
      "chunk_id": "LEGAL_VENDOR_LEGAL_GUIDELINES_CHUNK_002"
    }
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "LEGAL_VENDOR_LEGAL_GUIDELINES_CHUNK_003",
    "text": "The guidelines apply to vendors and prospective vendors whose relationships require legal or compliance review.",
    "metadata": {
      "department": "Legal",
      "document_name": "Vendor_Legal_Guidelines",
      "document_type": "DOCX",
      "source_file": "data/raw/Legal/Vendor_Legal_Guidelines.docx",
      "policy_title": "Vendor Legal and Compliance Guidelines",
      "version": "2026",
      "effective_date": "01-Apr-2026",
      "owner_department": "Legal",
      "document_id": "LEGAL_VENDOR_LEGAL_GUIDELINES",
      "section": "2. Scope",
      "chunk_id": "LEGAL_VENDOR_LEGAL_GUIDELINES_CHUNK_003"
    }
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "LEGAL_VENDOR_LEGAL_GUIDELINES_CHUNK_004",
    "text": "Legal review may consider vendor identity, ownership, regulatory status, contractual history, data handling, intellectual property, conflicts of interest, and other relevant risks.",
    "metadata": {
      "department": "Legal",
      "document_name": "Vendor_Legal_Guidelines",
      "document_type": "DOCX",
      "source_file": "data/raw/Legal/Vendor_Legal_Guidelines.docx",
      "policy_title": "Vendor Legal and Compliance Guidelines",
      "version": "2026",
      "effective_date": "01-Apr-2026",
      "owner_department": "Legal",
      "document_id": "LEGAL_VENDOR_LEGAL_GUIDELINES",
      "section": "3. Legal Due Diligence",
      "chunk_id": "LEGAL_VENDOR_LEGAL_GUIDELINES_CHUNK_004"
    }
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "LEGAL_VENDOR_LEGAL_GUIDELINES_CHUNK_005",
    "text": "Depending on the vendor category, relevant documentation may include registration records, tax information, certifications, compliance declarations, ownership details, data-protection information, and contract documentation.",
    "metadata": {
      "department": "Legal",
      "document_name": "Vendor_Legal_Guidelines",
      "document_type": "DOCX",
      "source_file": "data/raw/Legal/Vendor_Legal_Guidelines.docx",
      "policy_title": "Vendor Legal and Compliance Guidelines",
      "version": "2026",
      "effective_date": "01-Apr-2026",
      "owner_department": "Legal",
      "document_id": "LEGAL_VENDOR_LEGAL_GUIDELINES",
      "section": "4. Required Vendor Documentation",
      "chunk_id": "LEGAL_VENDOR_LEGAL_GUIDELINES_CHUNK_005"
    }
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "LEGAL_VENDOR_LEGAL_GUIDELINES_CHUNK_006",
    "text": "Non-standard vendor contracts require Legal review. Legal evaluates material terms, risk allocation, mandatory clauses, applicable laws, data protection, intellectual property, liability, termination, and dispute provisions.",
    "metadata": {
      "department": "Legal",
      "document_name": "Vendor_Legal_Guidelines",
      "document_type": "DOCX",
      "source_file": "data/raw/Legal/Vendor_Legal_Guidelines.docx",
      "policy_title": "Vendor Legal and Compliance Guidelines",
      "version": "2026",
      "effective_date": "01-Apr-2026",
      "owner_department": "Legal",
      "document_id": "LEGAL_VENDOR_LEGAL_GUIDELINES",
      "section": "5. Contract Review",
      "chunk_id": "LEGAL_VENDOR_LEGAL_GUIDELINES_CHUNK_006"
    }
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "LEGAL_VENDOR_LEGAL_GUIDELINES_CHUNK_007",
    "text": "Contracts involving organizational or personal data should address appropriate data protection obligations, security expectations, permitted use, incident handling, and relevant contractual protections.",
    "metadata": {
      "department": "Legal",
      "document_name": "Vendor_Legal_Guidelines",
      "document_type": "DOCX",
      "source_file": "data/raw/Legal/Vendor_Legal_Guidelines.docx",
      "policy_title": "Vendor Legal and Compliance Guidelines",
      "version": "2026",
      "effective_date": "01-Apr-2026",
      "owner_department": "Legal",
      "document_id": "LEGAL_VENDOR_LEGAL_GUIDELINES",
      "section": "6. Data Protection",
      "chunk_id": "LEGAL_VENDOR_LEGAL_GUIDELINES_CHUNK_007"
    }
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "LEGAL_VENDOR_LEGAL_GUIDELINES_CHUNK_008",
    "text": "Vendor arrangements involving software, content, technology, or deliverables should clearly address ownership or permitted use of intellectual property.",
    "metadata": {
      "department": "Legal",
      "document_name": "Vendor_Legal_Guidelines",
      "document_type": "DOCX",
      "source_file": "data/raw/Legal/Vendor_Legal_Guidelines.docx",
      "policy_title": "Vendor Legal and Compliance Guidelines",
      "version": "2026",
      "effective_date": "01-Apr-2026",
      "owner_department": "Legal",
      "document_id": "LEGAL_VENDOR_LEGAL_GUIDELINES",
      "section": "7. Intellectual Property",
      "chunk_id": "LEGAL_VENDOR_LEGAL_GUIDELINES_CHUNK_008"
    }
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "LEGAL_VENDOR_LEGAL_GUIDELINES_CHUNK_009",
    "text": "Vendor relationships should be screened for relevant regulatory obligations, conflicts of interest, required certifications, sanctions or compliance considerations where applicable, and other material legal risks.",
    "metadata": {
      "department": "Legal",
      "document_name": "Vendor_Legal_Guidelines",
      "document_type": "DOCX",
      "source_file": "data/raw/Legal/Vendor_Legal_Guidelines.docx",
      "policy_title": "Vendor Legal and Compliance Guidelines",
      "version": "2026",
      "effective_date": "01-Apr-2026",
      "owner_department": "Legal",
      "document_id": "LEGAL_VENDOR_LEGAL_GUIDELINES",
      "section": "8. Compliance",
      "chunk_id": "LEGAL_VENDOR_LEGAL_GUIDELINES_CHUNK_009"
    }
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "LEGAL_VENDOR_LEGAL_GUIDELINES_CHUNK_010",
    "text": "Single-source procurement may be appropriate for proprietary technology, specialized services, an only-qualified vendor, or other documented circumstances. The business justification and applicable approvals must be recorded.",
    "metadata": {
      "department": "Legal",
      "document_name": "Vendor_Legal_Guidelines",
      "document_type": "DOCX",
      "source_file": "data/raw/Legal/Vendor_Legal_Guidelines.docx",
      "policy_title": "Vendor Legal and Compliance Guidelines",
      "version": "2026",
      "effective_date": "01-Apr-2026",
      "owner_department": "Legal",
      "document_id": "LEGAL_VENDOR_LEGAL_GUIDELINES",
      "section": "9. Single-Source Procurement",
      "chunk_id": "LEGAL_VENDOR_LEGAL_GUIDELINES_CHUNK_010"
    }
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "LEGAL_VENDOR_LEGAL_GUIDELINES_CHUNK_011",
    "text": "High-risk vendors may require enhanced legal or compliance review before activation or contracting.",
    "metadata": {
      "department": "Legal",
      "document_name": "Vendor_Legal_Guidelines",
      "document_type": "DOCX",
      "source_file": "data/raw/Legal/Vendor_Legal_Guidelines.docx",
      "policy_title": "Vendor Legal and Compliance Guidelines",
      "version": "2026",
      "effective_date": "01-Apr-2026",
      "owner_department": "Legal",
      "document_id": "LEGAL_VENDOR_LEGAL_GUIDELINES",
      "section": "10. High-Risk Vendors",
      "chunk_id": "LEGAL_VENDOR_LEGAL_GUIDELINES_CHUNK_011"
    }
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "LEGAL_VENDOR_LEGAL_GUIDELINES_CHUNK_012",
    "text": "Legal may recommend suspension of a vendor where material legal or compliance concerns exist. Procurement may initiate a suspension review. These guidelines do not define a final approving authority for vendor suspension.",
    "metadata": {
      "department": "Legal",
      "document_name": "Vendor_Legal_Guidelines",
      "document_type": "DOCX",
      "source_file": "data/raw/Legal/Vendor_Legal_Guidelines.docx",
      "policy_title": "Vendor Legal and Compliance Guidelines",
      "version": "2026",
      "effective_date": "01-Apr-2026",
      "owner_department": "Legal",
      "document_id": "LEGAL_VENDOR_LEGAL_GUIDELINES",
      "section": "11. Compliance Issues and Suspension",
      "chunk_id": "LEGAL_VENDOR_LEGAL_GUIDELINES_CHUNK_012"
    }
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "LEGAL_VENDOR_LEGAL_GUIDELINES_CHUNK_013",
    "text": "Business owners provide accurate vendor context. Procurement manages commercial onboarding. Finance performs applicable financial verification. Legal performs legal and compliance review and provides recommendations.",
    "metadata": {
      "department": "Legal",
      "document_name": "Vendor_Legal_Guidelines",
      "document_type": "DOCX",
      "source_file": "data/raw/Legal/Vendor_Legal_Guidelines.docx",
      "policy_title": "Vendor Legal and Compliance Guidelines",
      "version": "2026",
      "effective_date": "01-Apr-2026",
      "owner_department": "Legal",
      "document_id": "LEGAL_VENDOR_LEGAL_GUIDELINES",
      "section": "12. Responsibilities",
      "chunk_id": "LEGAL_VENDOR_LEGAL_GUIDELINES_CHUNK_013"
    }
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "LEGAL_VENDOR_LEGAL_GUIDELINES_CHUNK_014",
    "text": "Exceptions must be documented and assessed for legal and compliance impact before approval.",
    "metadata": {
      "department": "Legal",
      "document_name": "Vendor_Legal_Guidelines",
      "document_type": "DOCX",
      "source_file": "data/raw/Legal/Vendor_Legal_Guidelines.docx",
      "policy_title": "Vendor Legal and Compliance Guidelines",
      "version": "2026",
      "effective_date": "01-Apr-2026",
      "owner_department": "Legal",
      "document_id": "LEGAL_VENDOR_LEGAL_GUIDELINES",
      "section": "13. Exceptions",
      "chunk_id": "LEGAL_VENDOR_LEGAL_GUIDELINES_CHUNK_014"
    }
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "LEGAL_VENDOR_LEGAL_GUIDELINES_CHUNK_015",
    "text": "2025 — Initial guidelines issued. 2026 — Legal due diligence, single-source, data protection, and vendor compliance guidance updated.",
    "metadata": {
